@startuml
' Toolchain proof and the shared legend style for the SAD.
' Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh. It is a small, illustrative fragment,
' not the delivered Components-and-Connectors view (that is authored in Slice 2).
!include style.puml
title Diagram key: notation legend (illustrative C&C fragment)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "POS system" as POS #dae8fc
component "Store Agent" as SA #d5e8d4
queue "Outbox" as OB #e1d5e7
component "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #fff2cc
component "Subscriber" as SUB #fff2cc

POS --> SA : <<external>>\nsales records
SA --> OB : append\n(store-and-forward)
OB --> CFE : publish\n[secure channel]
CFE --> SUB : notify\n(n-ary publish-subscribe)

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| rectangle, green fill | store-side runtime component |
| rectangle, yellow fill | distribution-center runtime component |
| queue shape, purple fill | durable, ordered persistent store |
| node, blue fill | external system / boundary element |
| solid arrow | connector; label names the protocol or interaction |
| [secure channel] | a store-to-DC connector that is a secure channel |
endlegend
@enduml
